{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Helvetica;}}\f0\fs24 {\b Topology}\par Google Docs (Lookup)\par draw.io (Modify)\par Google Docs (Create)\par \par {\b Request}\par Our payments service sometimes loses the webhooks the card processor sends us when a server restarts, so some payments get stuck as pending until someone fixes them by hand. I need to pick a design to fix this and get it written up for the team. In Google Docs I'll read the problem brief with the numbers and the three options we've talked about. In draw.io I'll open our current architecture diagram and update it with the option I pick: storing each webhook first, then a queue, a retry worker and a dead letter queue. Then back in Google Docs I'll write a short decision record with the option I chose, why I didn't pick the other two, and the risks. Deliverables are the updated diagram and the decision record as a PDF.\par \par {\b Task Description}\par 1. In Google Docs, read the problem brief and point out the numbers and limits that matter and the three options.\par 2. In draw.io, open the current architecture diagram and show where a webhook gets lost on a restart.\par 3. In draw.io, remove the in-memory background step, add the inbox table, queue, retry worker and dead letter queue from the shape panel, connect them and label each step.\par 4. In draw.io, save the diagram and export it as a PNG.\par 5. In Google Docs, fill in the decision record with the status, context, decision, why the other two options lost, and the risks and follow-ups.\par 6. In Google Docs, download the decision record as a PDF.\par }